{"id":"208076812","type":"page","ari":"ari:cloud:confluence:8702f96a-1aec-4506-80f6-c8b4c62822fc:page/208076812","base64EncodedAri":"YXJpOmNsb3VkOmNvbmZsdWVuY2U6ODcwMmY5NmEtMWFlYy00NTA2LTgwZjYtYzhiNGM2MjgyMmZjOmNvbnRlbnQvMjA4MDc2ODEy","status":"current","title":"Scales Splitting types: by volumes, by number of days","macroRenderedOutput":{},"body":{"storage":{"value":"<ol start=\"1\"><li><p><strong>Tarif scales splitting by scale codes&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Tariff scales </strong>in each sub period should be splitted if covers more than one scale code period. Should check if <strong>By number of days </strong>checkbox is checked in sales nomenclature for this tariff scale row and calculate new volumes according different formulas.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>By number of days&nbsp; - checked&nbsp;in in scales nomenclature</strong></p><p>New volume for each interval =<br />(tariff scale volume /number of days in tariff scale period)* number of days for each<br />splitted period</p><p><strong><ac:inline-comment-marker ac:ref=\"e0799d36-54d6-44ee-b75c-1c30862ae208\">By number of days - not checked&nbsp;checked&nbsp;in scales nomenclature</ac:inline-comment-marker></strong></p><p>New volume for each interval=&nbsp;&nbsp;(tariff scale volume /sum of all scale codes<br />from all periods) * sum of scale codes volumes for each period</p></li><li><p>For both calculation rounding should be done after splitting with General rounding rule:<ac:link ac:card-appearance=\"inline\"><ri:page ri:content-title=\"General rounding rules\" ri:version-at-save=\"3\" /><ac:link-body>General rounding rules</ac:link-body></ac:link> </p></li></ol><p><strong>&nbsp;Initial Data</strong></p><table data-table-width=\"1336\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"c593bb1c-be19-44c3-b2b0-de1d30e6389c\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 222.0px;\" /><col style=\"width: 222.0px;\" /><col style=\"width: 222.0px;\" /><col style=\"width: 222.0px;\" /><col style=\"width: 97.0px;\" /><col style=\"width: 347.0px;\" /></colgroup><tbody><tr><th data-highlight-colour=\"var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,#f1f2f4))\"><p><strong>scale code/tariff scale</strong></p></th><th data-highlight-colour=\"var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,#f1f2f4))\"><p><strong>start</strong></p></th><th data-highlight-colour=\"var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,#f1f2f4))\"><p><strong>End</strong></p></th><th data-highlight-colour=\"var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,#f1f2f4))\"><p><strong>By number of days</strong></p></th><th data-highlight-colour=\"var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,#f1f2f4))\"><p><strong>Volume</strong></p></th><th data-highlight-colour=\"var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,#f1f2f4))\"><p><strong><span style=\"background-color: rgb(211,241,167);\">Formula</span></strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p>code1</p></td><td><p>1 Sep</p></td><td><p>10 Sep</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>code1</p></td><td><p>11 Sep</p></td><td><p>20 Sep</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>20</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>code2</p></td><td><p>1 Sep</p></td><td><p>10 Sep</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>code2</p></td><td><p>11 Sep</p></td><td><p>20 Sep</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>20</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>tariff1</p></td><td><p>1 Sep</p></td><td><p>20 Sep</p></td><td><p>YES</p></td><td><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">200</span></p></td><td><p><strong><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">formula (YES) </span></strong><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">= (tariff scale volume /number of days tariff scale )* number of days for each splitted period</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">tariff scale volume = 200</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">number of days tariff scale = 20 Sep -1 Sep+1</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">number of days splitted period 1= 10 Sep-1 sep+1</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">number of days splitted period 2= 20 Sep-11 sep+1</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">volume for Period1 = 200/20*10= 50</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">volume for Period2 = 200/20*10= 50</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>tariff2</p></td><td><p>1 Sep</p></td><td><p>20 Sep</p></td><td><p>NO</p></td><td><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">200</span></p></td><td><p><strong><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">formula(NO) </span></strong><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">= (tariff scale volume /sum of all scale codes from all periods) * sum of scale codes volumes for each period</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">number of days tariff scale )* number of days for each splitted period</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">tariff scale volume = 100</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">sum of all scale codes from all periods = 60</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">sum of scale codes volumes for period1 =20</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">sum of scale codes volumes for period2=40</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">volume for Period1 = 200/60*20= 66.6667</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">volume for Period2 = 100/20*40= 133.3333</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p /><p><strong>Result</strong>: </p><table data-table-width=\"1336\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"eebdcbcb-c1fe-437f-8563-36717be03610\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 302.0px;\" /><col style=\"width: 301.0px;\" /><col style=\"width: 301.0px;\" /><col style=\"width: 301.0px;\" /><col style=\"width: 131.0px;\" /></colgroup><tbody><tr><th data-highlight-colour=\"var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,#f1f2f4))\"><p><strong>scale code/tariff scale</strong></p></th><th data-highlight-colour=\"var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,#f1f2f4))\"><p><strong>start</strong></p></th><th data-highlight-colour=\"var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,#f1f2f4))\"><p><strong>End</strong></p></th><th data-highlight-colour=\"var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,#f1f2f4))\"><p><strong>By number of days</strong></p></th><th data-highlight-colour=\"var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,var(--ds-background-accent-gray-subtlest,#f1f2f4))\"><p><strong>Volume</strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p>code1</p></td><td><p>1 Sep</p></td><td><p>10 Sep</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>10</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>code2</p></td><td><p>11 Sep</p></td><td><p>20 Sep</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>20</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>tariff1</p></td><td><p>1 Sep</p></td><td><p>10 Sep</p></td><td><p>YES</p></td><td><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">100</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>tariff1</p></td><td><p>11 Sep</p></td><td><p>20 Sep</p></td><td><p>YES</p></td><td><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">100</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>tariff2</p></td><td><p>1 Sep</p></td><td><p>10 Sep</p></td><td><p>NO</p></td><td><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">66.6667</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>tariff2</p></td><td><p>11 Sep</p></td><td><p>20 Sep</p></td><td><p>NO</p></td><td><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198,237,251);\">133.3333</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table>","representation":"storage","embeddedContent":[